# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Wave Rider Nusantara React + Vite game project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1`
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Installation Method**: `npm install @vercel/analytics`

### 2. Files Modified

#### `package.json`
- Added `@vercel/analytics: ^2.0.1` to dependencies

#### `package-lock.json`
- Updated with 160 new packages related to @vercel/analytics and its dependencies

#### `src/App.jsx`
- **Line 3**: Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
- **Line 702**: Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main JSX return statement (just before the closing `</div>` tag)

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection
- Project uses: React 19.2.0 with Vite 7.2.2
- Build tool: Vite with React SWC plugin
- Component structure: Functional components with hooks

### Configuration Approach
Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
1. Installed the package using npm
2. Imported the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/react'
3. Added the Analytics component to the main App component (WaveRiderGame)
4. Placed the component at the end of the JSX tree to ensure it doesn't interfere with existing game logic

### Placement Rationale
The `<Analytics />` component was placed:
- Inside the main container div of the WaveRiderGame component
- After all game UI elements (canvas, overlays, controls)
- Just before the closing tag to ensure it loads after critical game content
- This placement ensures analytics tracking without blocking game rendering

